<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Two halves, and they run the same way. One is the part of the shell that
    joins a compiled program to a sound device and touches no UI type at all;
    the other drives real controls through Avalonia's headless platform, which
    lays out and renders without a window server. Both are ordinary tests — see
    Ui/UiTest.cs for what a UI one costs.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Flyback.App\Flyback.App.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Flyback.Ui\Flyback.Ui.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Flyback.Viewer\Flyback.Viewer.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Shouldly" Version="4.3.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" Version="4.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Headless gives layout, input and rendering with no window server. The Skia
    reference is what makes CaptureRenderedFrame produce actual pixels rather
    than throwing: the default headless drawing backend does no rasterising, and
    a test that cannot see what it drew is the kind that passed while the number
    boxes in the step list rendered empty.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Headless" Version="12.1.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Skia" Version="12.1.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Fonts.Inter" Version="12.1.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Themes.Fluent" Version="12.1.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Headless/ is Avalonia.Headless.XUnit's own source (MIT, from
    src/Headless/Avalonia.Headless.XUnit in AvaloniaUI/Avalonia), compiled here
    instead of referenced as a package. The shipped assembly is built against
    xunit.v3 3.2.2 and its discoverer throws MissingMethodException on 4.x,
    which loses every UI test in this assembly at discovery; built from source
    it is compiled against whatever xunit the project uses.

    Kept as close to upstream as it can be, so a newer Avalonia can be diffed
    against it: what changed is the xunit 4 extensibility API it sits on — the
    scheduling values ISelfExecutingXunitTestCase.Run now carries, threaded down
    to the runner contexts, and a discoverer override whose signature moved. The
    four AvaloniaTestFramework* files are left out, being the assembly-attribute
    route that [AvaloniaFact] does not take.

    Delete the folder and reference the package again once Avalonia ships one
    built against xunit.v3 4.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Update="Headless\*.cs" Visible="true" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
